skos:narrower  a  owl:AnnotationProperty .

:R-HSA-9758274  a           owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0008150 ;
        rdfs:comment        "Nuclear factor kappa B (NF-kappa-B, NF-ÎºB) is activated by a diverse range of stimuli including cytokines, ligands of pattern-recognition receptors (PRRs) such as Toll-like receptors (TLRs) in myeloid cells, antigen-activated TCR in T-cells and by DNA damage (reviewed in Yu H et al. 2020; Zhang T et al. 2021). NF-kappa-B regulates the transcription of genes that are involved in immune and inflammatory responses, cell cycle, cell proliferation and apoptosis (Bhatt D & Ghosh S 2014; Liu T et al. 2017; Yu H et al. 2020). In unstimulated cells, NF-ÎºB is sequestered in the cytosol through interactions with a class of inhibitor proteins, called NF-ÎºB inhibitors (IkBs, such as NFKBIA or NFKBIB) (Jacobs MD & Harrison SC 1998). IkBs mask the nuclear localization signal (NLS) of NF-ÎºB preventing its nuclear translocation (Cervantes CF et al. 2011). A key event in NF-ÎºB activation involves phosphorylation of IkBs by the IÎºB kinase (IKK) complex which consists of CHUK, IKBKB and IKBKG subunits (IsraÃ«l A 2010). The activated NF-ÎºB signaling is tightly controlled at multiple levels (Dorrington MG & Fraser IDC 2019; Prescott JA et al. 2021). Dysregulated NF-ÎºB activity can cause tissue damage associated with inflammatory diseases and is also linked to tumorigenesis (Aggarwal BB & Sung B 2011; Liu T et al.2017; Barnabei L et al. 2021). The regulation of NF-ÎºB is cell-type-, context- , and stimulus-dependent and is crucial for orchestrating specific cellular responses (Mussbacher M et al. 2019).<p>This Reactome module describes several molecular mechanisms that regulate TLR-mediated NF-ÎºB signaling at the level of the IKK signaling complex. <br><br>" ;
        rdfs:label          "Regulation of NF-kappa B signaling" ;
        dc:contributor      "Reviewed: D'Eustachio, Peter, 2022-01-05" , "Edited: Shamovsky, Veronica, 2022-05-10" , "GOC:reactome_curators" , "Reviewed: de Martin, R, 2022-05-04" , "Authored: Shamovsky, Veronica, 2021-11-12" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-9758274" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-445989/R-HSA-445989> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

